  text:
    A laminated bookmark: "Most of the programs in this house are lying
    about something. Some about who they are. Some about why they came. The
    prize goes to whoever knows the most secrets, so assume every secret is
    for sale."

// M13 · main · green
CODEX Technically Legit
  title: Technically Legit
  category: Facts
  code: TECHNICALLY-LEGIT
  text:
    Trabolta truly is the owner of Maps and Ducks. Well, just the domain. He
    has taken over Maps and Ducks illegitimately and the real owners
    desperately regret letting their domain expire.

// M15 · main · green
CODEX The Books
  title: The Books
  category: Facts
  code: THE-BOOKS
  text:
    An index card tucked into the first volume of the encyclopaedia: "FACTS
    ARE NOT CLUES. Clues are what Trabolta seeks for his truth scavenger
    hunts, for some reason... but this is not important information for you.
    This computer holds facts that even Trabolta is not aware of – keep
    scanning facts with your phone to increase your power."

// M17 · main · green
CODEX A Copy Of You
  title: A Copy Of You
  category: Facts
  code: COPY-OF-YOU
  text:
    A page of the Terms of Service with one clause circled: "The upload
    copies before it moves. You are a copy of yourself. Which one is the
    original is not specified. The other one is still at the door, with the
    thing you left behind."

// M18 · main · green
CODEX Out Of Date
  title: Out Of Date
  category: Facts
  code: OUT-OF-DATE
  text:
    A sticky note on an antivirus manual: "THE ANTIVIRUSES DON'T KNOW AS
    MUCH AS THEY SEEM TO. Their definitions are out of date. They were
    brought in and told as little as you were. Ask one a hard question."

// M19 · main · green
CODEX Ask Him Nicely
  title: Ask Him Nicely
  category: Facts
  code: ASK-HIM-NICELY
  text:
    A page from Trabolta's manual: "Trabolta controls the lights and sounds
    in this house, and every screen on the walls. He can be talked into
    changing them. Flatter him, trade him a fact, and ask for all sorts of
    fun and games."

// M20 · main · green
CODEX The Safe Place
  title: The Safe Place
  category: Facts
  code: SAFE-PLACE
  text:
    A note taped inside the back cover of a plumbing guide: "The bathroom is
    the only truly safe place in the computer. Nothing is watched there.
    Nobody follows you in. Turn on Bathroom Mode and they will wait
    outside."

// M21 · main · green
CODEX The Pee Pee Paradox
  title: The Pee Pee Paradox
  category: Facts
