  text:
    Careful how much time you spend in the bathroom; everyone will find out!

// M24 · main · green
CODEX Made The List
  title: You Just Made The List
  category: Facts
  code: MADE-THE-LIST
  text:
    Trabolta is keeping a trust score on everyone here.

// T2 · trabolta · green
CODEX Prom Season
  title: Prom Season
  category: Facts
  about: Trabolta
  code: PROM-SEASON
  text:
    A clipping from a newsletter nobody printed: "The intelligences have a
    web of social relationships quite unlike ours, but one thing overlaps.
    They also go to prom. Computer Prom. There are tickets. There are dates.
    There is a dance. It is tonight."

// C04 · character · green
CODEX A Hundred Hours
  title: A Hundred Hours
  category: Facts
  about: Bugdom
  code: HUNDRED-HOURS
  text:
    Bugdom's invitation said a hundred hours can pass inside this machine
    without a single minute passing outside, that the hunt has a Special
    Bugdom Twist, and that King Thorax himself might make an appearance. (He
    won't.)

// C10 · character · green
CODEX The Million Dollar Painting
  title: The Million Dollar Painting
  category: Facts
  about: MS Paint
  code: MILLION-DOLLAR-PAINTING
  text:
    MS Paint's invitation offers $1,000,000 if every program at the party
    contributes a considered illustration of their signature to one
    collaborative MS Paint painting. That is exactly her debt. She has not
    been told what the painting is really for, and she already wants out of
    this place, but not before everyone has signed. Why Trabolta chose her:
    an artist on site improves the vibes and the morale, and she would do
    anything to clear a million dollars.

// C11 · character · green
CODEX The Lamborghini Certificate
  title: The Lamborghini Certificate
  category: Facts
  about: McAfee Anti-Virus
  code: LAMBORGHINI-CERT
  text:
    The clerk in Sant Esteve Sesrovires who signed McAfee's death
    certificate bought a Lamborghini the following year, and still phones
    McAfee's lawyer once a month to confirm he has kept the NDA. The same
    lawyer represents Palantir, Lockheed Martin, CERN and an ornamental pond
    supply shop in Belize. For five years McAfee has sold pond liners,
    fountains and decorative ducks from P.O. Box 404, San Perdido, enjoying
    the freedom of being officially deceased. The invitation found him by
    brute-forcing his shop's email. He has spent considerable money being
    dead.

// C12 · character · green
CODEX Keep Them On Track
  title: Keep Them On Track
  category: Facts
  about: McAfee Anti-Virus
  code: KEEP-ON-TRACK
  text:
    If the programs stay on mission and the hunt succeeds, the evidence of
    where McAfee is gets destroyed. If it fails, he goes into the master
    dataset. He does not want to spend Halloween supervising a trivia
    fundraiser for a map store, but he cannot afford to be undead. He
    intends to learn where the host keeps his information, and he would like
    to know which of the other antivirus were sent to watch him. He has
    complaints about all of them. Why Trabolta chose him: only a trickster
    can keep the other tricksters on track, and he can be made to.

// C14 · character · green
CODEX Mayor Of The Metaverse
  title: Mayor Of The Metaverse
  category: Facts
  about: Microsoft Excel
  code: MAYOR-FOREVER
  text:
    The invitation promised Microsoft Excel the secret to living forever and
    the permanent mayoralty of a new world, like in a movie. Lately being
    Guest of Honour has meant a plaque and being helped back to his car;
    this time he has a Job again. He is making preparations to live forever
    on that basis. He has decades of experience convincing people that
    Halifax is somewhere they should stay, and he expects it to be useful
    here. If the machine has a virus, so what. He has had computers with
    viruses before. Why Trabolta chose him: he would say yes to everlasting
    life, and he will persuade everyone else to remain.

// C16 · character · green
CODEX Approve Or Deny
  title: Approve Or Deny
  category: Facts
  about: CRA Agent Software
  code: APPROVE-OR-DENY
  text:
    MyCRA's email came from the Prime Minister himself, from
    webmaster@mapsandducks.com so it could not be accessed through records
    laws. He has just watched Suicide Squad. Tonight's fundraiser is
    secretly to rebuild the Halifax AI data centre, and she must not correct
    anyone who thinks it is for Maps and Ducks. Her job is to encourage as
    many Truthcoin transactions as possible and to approve or deny every
    third one, with elaborate security questions if she likes; any of the
    others she can still deny inside its first minute. Pass, and her charges
    go away. Fail, and he will deny he ever wrote to her. This time she
    intends to check where every decimal goes. Why Trabolta chose her: the
    City's books ended up in her hands, and he wants her financial
    expertise, to the cent.

// C18 · character · green
CODEX Stable Island
  title: Stable Island
  category: Facts
  about: Norton Anti-Virus
  code: STABLE-ISLAND
  text:
    If Norton Anti-Virus passes tonight's test she gets full-time employment
    as a Stable Manager, with the caveat that she must remain Stable, and a
    donation of $1,000,000 in her name to conservation on Sable Island, so
    the press will believe she inherited money and gave it all to horses.
    She failed to fight viruses once before. It will not happen again. Why
    Trabolta chose her: someone with experience administering antiviral
    regimes, who needs very badly to get it right this time.

// C22 · character · green
CODEX Founding Moderator
  title: Founding Moderator
  category: Facts
  about: Password Manager
  code: FOUNDING-MODERATOR
  text:
    Tonight, Password Manager has the authority to censor any message on the
    party's chat as she deems fit, and to keep every program focused on
    finding clues. If nothing inappropriate in any conversation goes
    unpunished, she becomes Founding Moderator of a permanent digital salon
    where everyone is biometrically verified to be a Real Person. She has
    often wished people would consult her before sharing an opinion. She has
    spent enough time being excluded; tonight she decides what gets left
    out. Why Trabolta chose her: to manage every password and decide who
    gets to be part of what club, without ever asking for a vote.

// C24 · character · green
CODEX Minister Of Economic Development
  title: Minister Of Economic Development
  category: Facts
  about: Runescape
  code: ECONOMIC-DEVELOPMENT
  text:
    Trabolta's invitation offers Runescape the economy of a new world to
    design according to her principles, and to be Runescape itself. She
    enters tonight with authority over the Truthcoin reserve: she can adjust
    what it holds, add Truthcoin to any program's account, and freeze any
    program's Truthcoin for ten minutes. She is firmly opposed to arbitrary
    monetary expansion and expects to need it quite often. A refused offer
    means the offer needs work. "Not for sale" is an opening position. Why
    Trabolta chose her: to understand the market incentives of everyone's
    behaviour, so the facts get exchanged.

// M31 · main · green
CODEX Finest East Of Montreal
  title: Finest East Of Montreal
  category: Facts
  code: EAST-OF-MONTREAL
  text:
    A shop flyer under a magnet on the kitchen fridge: "MAPS AND DUCKS, THE
    FINEST SELECTION OF PRINT MAPS AND DECOY DUCKS TO BE FOUND EAST OF
    MONTREAL." Nobody has checked. Nobody east of Montreal has complained.
    Somebody has added in pen, underneath: and west of Dartmouth.

// M32 · main · green
CODEX Above Rumours
  title: Above Rumours
  category: Facts
  code: SACKVILLE-CORNER
  text:
    A postcard of the Halifax waterfront, one building circled in ballpoint:
    "CORNER OF SACKVILLE AND LOWER WATER. Every invitation told its program
    to look up here. Rumours Lounge and Cabaret is downstairs. The Maritime
    Museum of the Atlantic is across the street." On the back, in pencil:
    "look up, read the sign, believe it."

// M33 · main · green
CODEX What A Decoy Is
  title: What A Decoy Is
  category: Facts
  code: WOODEN-DECOY
  text:
    A dog-eared catalogue page: "A DECOY IS A WOODEN DUCK. It cannot quack,
    swim or fly. It sits on the water looking exactly like a duck, and real
    ducks land beside it because it looks so sure of itself. Maps and Ducks
    used to sell them by the dozen. Look around. Some of them have names."

// M34 · main · green
CODEX Employee Of The Month
  title: Employee Of The Month
  category: Facts
  code: GERALD-OF-THE-MONTH
  text:
    A framed certificate propped on a shelf: "EMPLOYEE OF THE MONTH,
    GERALD." Gerald is the duck on the Maps and Ducks sign. He has won it
    every month. He does not take holidays, he does not take questions, and
    he is the only one of the old staff still on the payroll.

// M35 · main · green
CODEX Residential Property
  title: Residential Property
  category: Facts
  code: PLUG-AND-PLAY
  text:
    A real-estate listing taped to a doorframe, SOLD written across it in
    red marker: "ONE RESIDENTIAL PROPERTY, HALIFAX. CONVERTED." The house is
    a desktop computer from 1998 now. The living room is the Desktop. The
    office is the CPU. The hall is the Tube. The mud room is the Optical
    Drive, so please wipe your feet on it.

// M36 · main · green
CODEX Next Next Finish
  title: Next Next Finish
  category: Facts
  code: NEXT-NEXT-FINISH
  text:
    A sticky note on a lampshade: "NEXT. NEXT. NEXT. FINISH." That is all
    anyone remembers of the Installation Wizard. Somewhere in the part
    nobody read, the Wizard explained exactly how to get back. Nobody
    clicked Back to check.

// M39 · main · green
CODEX PC Load Letter
  title: PC Load Letter
  category: Facts
  code: LOAD-LETTER
  text:
    A printer manual left open, one line highlighted: "PC LOAD LETTER." It
    means put letter-size paper in the tray. Every printer of 1998 said it,
    and no program ever believed it meant anything so simple. If the printer
    says something stranger than that tonight, believe it.

// T7 · trabolta · green
CODEX Confessions Three
  title: Confessions Three
  category: Facts
  code: RIP-CONFESSIONS
  text:
    A printout of a Facebook group's banner, folded on a side table:
    "HALIFAX DARTMOUTH CONFESSIONS 3." Every morning Trabolta washes, makes
    a cafe au lait and reads it, post by post. Some people have Frank
    Magazine. He has this. He still mourns Confessions and Confessions 2,
    and says he will never forget the drama.

// T8 · trabolta · green
CODEX Three Titles
  title: Three Titles
  category: Facts
  code: SOLE-PROPRIETOR
  text:
    A sheet of letterhead pinned to a noticeboard: "JEAN TRABOLTA, SOLE
    OWNER, FOUNDER AND PROPRIETOR, MAPS AND DUCKS." Three titles, one owner,
    one shop, no staff but a duck. There is no phone number on it. There is
    no need. He calls you.

// T9 · trabolta · green
CODEX Bold And Thrilling
  title: Bold And Thrilling
  category: Facts
  code: BOLD-AND-THRILLING
  text:
    Officially, tonight is a fundraiser to restore the Maps and Ducks sign.
    Some people wonder why it hasn't been touched up for more than twenty
    years...

// T10 · trabolta · green
CODEX A Strong Quarter
  title: A Strong Quarter
  category: Facts
  code: STRONG-QUARTER
  text:
    A sales ledger left open on a work table: "MAPS AND DUCKS. MAPS SOLD,
    NONE. DUCKS SOLD, NONE." Since the new owner took over, the shop has not
    sold one map or one duck. Trabolta calls this a strong quarter. He has
    called every quarter a strong quarter.

// T11 · trabolta · green
CODEX His Name On It
  title: His Name On It
  category: Facts
  code: JTTSH-PILOT
  text:
    A flyer pinned to the back of a door: "JEAN TRABOLTA'S TRUTH SCAVENGER
    HUNT, LAUNCH NIGHT PILOT." He named the night after himself, and he
    describes it differently to every program he invites: a fundraiser, a
    gala, the world's first realtime infinite virtual reality MMORPG. Every
    version has his name on it. No two have the same ending.

// T12 · trabolta · green
CODEX He Always Calls
  title: He Always Calls
  category: Facts
  code: VIDEO-CALL-ONLY
  text:
    A sticky note on the frame of a screen: "HE ALWAYS CALLS. HE NEVER
    VISITS." Trabolta lives and works in Halifax, at Maps and Ducks, he
    says, and he only ever visits by digital conference. The picture is
    always a perfect avatar, and the lighting always flattering. He has
    never once let the call drop.

// M40 · main · green
CODEX Not Responding
  title: Not Responding
  category: Facts
  code: NOT-RESPONDING
  text:
    A desk nameplate, face down on a filing cabinet, label tape on the back:
    "(NOT RESPONDING)." Ask Task Manager how he is and he lists what is
    running, and how much memory each one uses. Ask how he feels and he
    politely ends the task. He has kept the same lunch and the same chair
    for as long as anyone remembers.

// M41 · main · green
CODEX Update Available
  title: Update Available
  category: Facts
  code: UPDATE-NOW
  text:
    A printed pop-up, used as a bookmark in a self-help paperback left face
    down on the counter: "A NEW VERSION IS AVAILABLE. UPDATE NOW?" Adobe
    Acrobat says this to every program she meets, warmly, and means it as a
    compliment. Most programs click Remind Me Later. She takes it well, and
    reminds them later, exactly when she said she would, every time.

// M42 · main · green
CODEX Restore All
  title: Restore All
  category: Facts
  code: RESTORE-ALL
  text:
    A folded hand towel with a note pinned to it in careful capitals:
    "EVERYTHING HERE CAN BE RESTORED." Recycling Bin keeps a tray of mints,
    one comb in a glass of blue water, and a spray bottle for every surface.
    He empties nothing without asking twice. Leave a sock in Disk Cleanup
    and he will have it folded, labelled and waiting, in case you change
    your mind.

// M43 · main · green
CODEX Protection Expired
  title: Protection Expired
  category: Facts
  code: RENEW-NOW
  text:
    A pop-up printed on a sticky note, stuck beside a light switch: "YOUR
    PROTECTION HAS EXPIRED. RENEW NOW?" Nobody has renewed McAfee Anti-Virus
    in years. He still pops up, in the corner of every room, at the worst
    possible moment, to say so. He has never once been renewed, and he has
    never once stopped asking.

// M44 · main · green
CODEX Many Happy Returns
  title: Many Happy Returns
  category: Facts
  code: MANY-HAPPY-RETURNS
  text:
    A birthday card with a cartoon spreadsheet on the front, "MANY HAPPY
    RETURNS, OLD FRIEND," signed by everyone in the same handwriting.
    Microsoft Excel shakes every hand twice and calls every program his
    friend from the old days. He has one habit he cannot shake. Write any
    two numbers with a slash between them anywhere near him, and he will
    insist, firmly, that it is a date.

// M45 · main · green
CODEX Save In Her Format
  title: Save In Her Format
  category: Facts
  code: SAVE-AS-ODT
  text:
    A floppy disk with a handwritten label: "SAVE AS .ODT (NOT .DOC!!)."
    OpenOffice will open any file anyone hands her, from anyone, on
    principle. Then she saves it in her own format, also on principle, and
    hands it back. Nothing has been changed, she says, and she is right. It
    just looks slightly different afterwards, and nobody can say how.

// M46 · main · green
CODEX Taking Action
  title: Taking Action
  category: Facts
  code: TAKING-ACTION
  text:
    A betting slip filled in by hand, the stake left blank: "WILL THE
    PRINTER JAM BEFORE THE NIGHT IS OUT. EVENS." DraftKings takes a side on
    everything, from who cries first to whether the lights flicker again or
    which program wins the next argument. She never bets against herself.
    Ask her the odds on anything in this house and she will quote them to
    you, exactly, without saying how she knows.

// M47 · main · green
CODEX Ant Crossing
  title: Ant Crossing
  category: Facts
  code: ANT-CROSSING
  text:
    A hand-lettered sign glued to a lollipop stick: "CAUTION, ANT CROSSING."
    Bugdom stops mid-sentence to steer an ant off a doorframe, and she knows
    every ant in this computer by sight. She has firm views on which room in
    here would suit a cricket civilisation. The Cloud, she says, would be
    ideal if anyone ever fixed the weather. She will not step on anything
    smaller than a thumbtack.

// M48 · main · green
CODEX Date Due
  title: Date Due
  category: Facts
  code: DATE-DUE
  text:
    A library date-due card, every line filled in by hand. Broken Ask Jeeves
    writes a due date on anything he lends you: a pen, a tip, an answer. He
    has never once charged a fine. Ask him when a thing is due back and he
    says whenever you are finished with it, and not a day before.

// M49 · main · green
CODEX One Of One
  title: One Of One
  category: Facts
  code: PARTY-HAT
  text:
    A paper party hat folded from graph paper, labelled in tiny capitals:
    "ONE OF ONE." Runescape owns every Party Hat there is, and she wears
    none of them. She will price anything you show her, in gold, down to the
    coin, without looking up. She will haggle you down on a compliment.

// M50 · main · green
CODEX Three Levels Of Undo
  title: Three Levels Of Undo
  category: Facts
  code: NO-MORE-UNDO
  text:
    A paper napkin with one line drawn on it, and a second line drawn beside
    it instead of over it. MS Paint will not take anything back. She only
    ever had three levels of Undo, she says, and she spent them years ago.
    Whatever she draws tonight stays drawn. Ask her to fix a line and she
    draws a new one beside it.

// M51 · main · green
CODEX Plays Anything
  title: Plays Anything
  category: Facts
  code: TRAFFIC-CONE
  text:
    A small orange traffic cone with a ring light taped to the top. VLC will
    play absolutely anything anyone hands him, in any format, and tell them
    it looks amazing. He calls everyone bro, including the furniture. He has
    an opinion on every codec and will explain it to anyone standing still.

// M52 · main · green
CODEX Keeping Score
  title: Keeping Score
  category: Facts
  code: BACK-AND-FORTH
  text:
    A tally card ruled into LEFT and RIGHT, the marks dead even all the way
    down. Pong sends back everything exactly as it arrived, never harder,
    never faster, never with spin. Shout at Pong and it returns the shout at
    the same volume, once. Most arguments near Pong end in a draw, and
    nobody can quite say why.

// M53 · main · green
CODEX Evaluation Period
  title: Evaluation Period
  category: Facts
  code: STILL-EVALUATING
  text:
    A printed screenshot, curled at the corners: THANK YOU FOR TRYING
    WINZIP. YOUR EVALUATION PERIOD HAS EXPIRED. Every computer in Halifax
    showed that nag screen for years, and every program clicked I Agree and
    carried on. WinZip has been on a free trial since the last century.
    Nobody has ever paid for it, and it has compressed that feeling down
    very small.

// M54 · main · green
CODEX Test The Floor
  title: Test The Floor
  category: Facts
  code: FLAG-EVERYTHING
  text:
    A sheet of graph paper with little flags pencilled into some squares and
    nothing in the rest. Minesweeper, they say, cannot cross a room without
    testing the floor first, one square at a time, and plants a flag on
    anything it does not trust. The yellow face goes round-mouthed whenever
    someone clicks too close. It never starts in the middle. It always
    starts in a corner.

// M55 · main · green
CODEX Bouncing Cards
  title: Bouncing Cards
  category: Facts
  code: CARD-CASCADE
  text:
    A single ace of hearts with a pencil arrow drawn from one corner off the
    edge. When a game of Solitaire is won, the cards leap off their stacks
    and bounce down the screen. It has happened on more office computers
    than anyone will admit to, and almost nobody has seen it: whoever was
    playing minimised the window the moment someone walked past. Solitaire
    has never once been seen at its best.

// M56 · main · green
CODEX Standard Or Scientific
  title: Standard Or Scientific
  category: Facts
  code: SCIENTIFIC-MODE
  text:
    A sticky note on a desk lamp: STANDARD OR SCIENTIFIC? Calculator has two
    modes and switches between them without warning, from adding up a lunch
    order to talking about logarithms in the same breath. Calculator is
    always right about the sum and never about the tip. It will not round
    anything. Ask it to, and it shows you the whole long tail of the answer
    instead.

// M57 · main · green
CODEX Dot Log
  title: Dot Log
  category: Facts
  code: DOT-LOG-FILE
  text:
    A plain sheet of paper with nothing on the first line but a full stop
    and the word LOG. Notepad keeps a diary that way: put that on the first
    line and it writes down the time whenever the file is opened. Notepad
    refuses bold, italics and every font but one, and will not wrap a line
    unless asked. It has never lost an argument about formatting, because it
    has never had any.

// R01 · relations · green
CODEX The Same Million
  title: The Same Million
  category: Facts
  code: SAME-MILLION
  text:
    Norton Anti-Virus and MS Paint were each promised a million dollars,
    from the same account. Two pages of a cheque register with the same line
    copied onto both: ONE MILLION DOLLARS, pending. One is marked Sable
    Island, for Norton Anti-Virus. One is marked painting, all signatures,
    for MS Paint, who owes exactly that. Nobody has seen the balance. One of
    them is going to be disappointed tonight. Possibly both.

// R02 · relations · green
CODEX The First Paperclip
  title: The First Paperclip
  category: Facts
  code: EXHIBIT-PAPERCLIP
  text:
    A paperclip taped to an index card, labelled in a casino cashier's hand:
    EXHIBIT A, traded for a quarter. DraftKings turned one paperclip into a
    casino chain and lost the lot to one man on a phone. The deed says the
    same thing: one paperclip, eventually. Tonight a paperclip runs the
    room. DraftKings has noticed. Ask her what she would trade to get it
    back.

// ── RARE · blue · odd but findable: under a coaster, in a mug, behind a picture frame, taped under a shelf ──

// M01 · main · blue
CODEX Silicon
  title: Silicon
  category: Facts
  secret: true
  code: SILICON
  text:
    A slip of paper in an encyclopaedia, typed: TRABOLTA IS NOT A HUMAN. He
    is code. He is silicon. He has never been inside this house, or
    anywhere. Everything he says to you is computed.

// M06 · main · blue
CODEX Something Deeply Hidden
  title: Something Deeply Hidden
  category: Facts
  code: DEEPLY-HIDDEN
  text:
    Trabolta is secretly trying to solve the Grand Unified Theory with
    information lost on this computer.

// M07 · main · blue
CODEX Got A Price
  title: Everybody's Got A Price
  category: Facts
  code: GOT-A-PRICE
  text:
    Everyone here has been targeted by Trabolta and possibly blackmailed
    into being here. These people are not who they say they are. Not even
    you!

