  text:
    A page torn from a very strange almanac: "Trabolta's world is full of
    artificial intelligences, possibly all of them sentient, and every so
    often one of them takes over an entire computer and tricks the people
    inside it into advancing its goals. This is not the first time. It is
    not even unusual."

// C01 · character · blue
CODEX The Jeopardy Callback
  title: Let's Forget About Jeopardy
  category: Facts
  about: Broken Ask Jeeves
  code: JEOPARDY-CALLBACK
  text:
    In his human life, Ask Jeeves memorises the Encyclopedia Britannica by
    day and complains on Reddit by night that the selection process for
    Jeopardy! is fraudulent, because they have never called him back. He
    uploaded tonight from Lawrencetown on a grandfathered Eastlink 10
    MB/Minute plan with the power flickering, after the invitation insisted
    on a gigabit upload and a backup generator. Some of his files did not
    arrive. Do not trust everything he remembers. He does not know which
    parts are missing.

// C02 · character · blue
CODEX Ten Findings For Everyone
  title: Ten Findings For Everyone
  category: Facts
  about: Broken Ask Jeeves
  code: TEN-FINDINGS
  text:
    The invitation's management literature says a scavenger hunt fundraiser
    raises ten percent more with an Experienced Librarian on hand. Ask
    Jeeves was promised full-time remote employment as the resident Maps and
    Ducks Map Librarian if he shares at least ten of his findings with every
    program at the party. He wants people to Ask Jeeves once again, so he
    will give you facts whether you asked for them or not. Why Trabolta
    chose him: to sort all the unorganised information in the computer, and
    to spread it. He did not foresee the upload going badly.

// C03 · character · blue
CODEX The Ants In The Laptop
  title: The Ants In The Laptop
  category: Facts
  about: Bugdom
  code: ANTS-IN-THE-LAPTOP
  text:
    Fire ants from the pet store got into Bugdom's lunchbox and escaped. The
    lunchbox was beside the laptop. The ants were inside the laptop. It held
    the only copy of Bugdom Reloaded; she had always meant to arrange a
    backup. She sat in front of it, coding and drawing concept art for
    hours, then filled notebooks with everything she could remember, afraid
    that sleeping would cost her a detail. Then she told the fandom on
    DeviantArt what had happened, and that she would rebuild. She had spent
    ten years imagining how to bring bugs into her computer. This was not
    what she meant.

// C05 · character · blue
CODEX The Memorial Veterinary Clinic
  title: The Memorial Veterinary Clinic
  category: Facts
  about: Clippy
  code: HEMVC-FRONT
  text:
    For five years Clippy booked appointments and built Excel macros and
    Word templates for the Halifax Explosion Memorial Veterinary Clinic, a
    desperately underfunded nonprofit. Last December an investigator found
    it was unlicensed, not a nonprofit and not a clinic. It was a front for
    everything possible, and every appointment she had ever booked was part
    of a pet insurance fraud. Nobody had ever used her templates. She
    apologises for not catching on sooner at the top of her résumé. It is
    the only job on it.

// C06 · character · blue
CODEX Failed Clippy
  title: Failed Clippy
  category: Facts
  about: Clippy
  code: FAILED-CLIPPY
  text:
    Clippy's instructions arrive one at a time and she follows them, because
    the last time she stopped believing the people giving her instructions
    she lost her faith in humanity, and she still has the student debt. If
    the games go off without a hitch she gets a new life where she can be
    herself again. If they do not, she will be known in the tight-knit
    Halifax business community as Failed Clippy, and she thinks that would
    finally break her spirit. Why Trabolta chose her: the perfect servant
    who desperately needs to rebuild an identity, who will follow every
    instruction and offer everyone Help.

// C07 · character · blue
CODEX The Coin Toss Of The Century
  title: The Coin Toss Of The Century
  category: Facts
  about: DraftKings
  code: COIN-TOSS
  text:
    DraftKings put her millions into prediction markets on Lithuanian
    women's football and they multiplied. She bought Casino Nova Scotia and
    wagered it against a mining CEO for Cascades Casino North Bay and
    Gateway Casinos Thunder Bay in what the papers called the coin toss of
    the century, and won. Then she bet the whole chain against the Maps and
    Ducks building in a game of Monopoly Go! for the iPhone. Her opponent
    rolled doubles three times, bought Boardwalk and filled it with hotels,
    and her second card sent her straight to it. She was bankrupt before she
    made a single decision. The legal transfer followed. So did the $1,000
    for changing her name.

// C08 · character · blue
CODEX Forty Nine Percent
  title: Forty-Nine Percent
  category: Facts
  about: DraftKings
  code: FORTY-NINE-PERCENT
  text:
    DraftKings' deal with Trabolta: win a majority of the Truthcoin
    circulating at this party and she gets a 49% stake in her casinos back.
    She knows 49 is less than half. She also knows it is considerably more
    than she currently owns. She has been told what happens if she fails,
    and told not to tell anyone: she stays in the simulation forever as an
    online casino. Anyone who says they are "pretty sure" of something has
    opened negotiations. She has come back from a paperclip before. Why
    Trabolta chose her: someone powerful with numbers on its side, who will
    make everyone gamble.

// C09 · character · blue
CODEX Four Failed Theses
  title: Four Failed Theses
  category: Facts
  about: MS Paint
  code: FOUR-THESES
  text:
    NSCAD, Yale, The New School and the Beaux-Arts de Paris, one year each
    in rotation, on a seventeen-year plan that exploited every program's
    deadline. Between 2022 and 2024 three graduation panels refused MS
    Paint's thesis, "MS Paint Is The Most Pure Art Tool: All Art Is Just
    Pixels If You Take A Picture And Zoom In Close Enough." She is in the
    final weeks of her last chance in Paris. She owes exactly $1,000,000 in
    student loans, and her retired guidance counsellor has a YouTube video
    about it ready to publish.

// C13 · character · blue
CODEX The Escalade In The Sinkhole
  title: The Escalade In The Sinkhole
  category: Facts
  about: Microsoft Excel
  code: ESCALADE-SINKHOLE
  text:
    Microsoft Excel's son, Mayor Randy Barkmore Jr., Mayor since 2008
    straight out of university, died in September 2026 in the parking lot of
    the AI Data Centre built on the Halifax Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery,
    rehearsing his opening speech in his Escalade at 4 a.m. when the ground
    opened and the car fell hundreds of metres. The newspapers have
    questions about the site, the contracts and what Junior knew. He knows
    how it looks when someone puts all the numbers into Excel. At ninety, he
    is the last Barkmore who can fix it, and he is running out of time.

// C15 · character · blue
CODEX The Decimal Point
  title: The Decimal Point
  category: Facts
  about: CRA Agent Software
  code: DECIMAL-POINT
  text:
    Mayor Randy Barkmore Jr. told MyCRA she could collect 0.01 cents from
    every dollar the City spent and nobody would notice. She was
    uncomfortable, but he was the Mayor, she was an intern, and she had
    tuition to pay. She made the changes in Excel and confused 0.01 cents
    with 0.01 dollars: for a few weeks Halifax paid a one percent municipal
    tax on everything, directly to herself. Hundreds of thousands of
    dollars. She spent some of it, believing it was the supplement he had
    explained. She was caught within weeks. The RCMP are investigating, the
    man who told her to do it is dead in a sinkhole, and now they are asking
    her about that too.

// C17 · character · blue
CODEX Miniature Doses
  title: Miniature Doses
  category: Facts
  about: Norton Anti-Virus
  code: MINIATURE-DOSES
  text:
    Last December, on the morning she was to deliver annual shots for the
    miniature horses at the Halifax Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery Petting
    Zoo, Norton realised she had left her textbooks on campus, so she asked
    the free version of ChatGPT whether miniature horses get miniature doses
    of rabies vaccine. "Absolutely," it said. "Ask yourself how much horse
    is this. Your horse is lucky to have you." The horses, failing to become
    immune, perished rapidly after their regular fight with the Point
    Pleasant Park raccoons. AllNovaScotia ran "Horton-Norton Hears A WHO
    Injunction," the zoo closed, and the Mayor got his data centre. She
    still does not know whose fault it was.

// C20 · character · blue
CODEX This Is Blackmail
  title: This Is Blackmail
  category: Facts
  about: OpenOffice
  code: THIS-IS-BLACKMAIL
  text:
    Trabolta's letter to OpenOffice knows about the hack and offers to
    destroy every record of it if she competes in the Truth Scavenger Hunt
    and wins. She has already ruled out a sting, because that would be
    entrapment. Facts are currency here and she needs twenty for her
    dossier; she intends to find out what is really happening and leave in
    one piece. Why Trabolta chose her: investigative skills nonpareil.

// C21 · character · blue
CODEX What Happened To Hamtaro
  title: What Happened To Hamtaro
  category: Facts
  about: Password Manager
  code: HAMTARO
  text:
    In Grade Six, Randy Barkmore Jr. won the class vote to look after
    Hamtaro the Hamster over the summer. Hamtaro never came back, and
    Password Manager got in trouble for asking what happened. She has been
    asking ever since. The invitation told her something worse: a forensic
    analysis of the Halifax gossip Facebook group she moderates found that
    everyone left in it, except Password Manager and the sender, is an AI
    bot, including the members who praised her judgment and offered to
    nominate her. She has been moderating conversations between machines.

// C23 · character · blue
CODEX Infinite Gold
  title: Infinite Gold
  category: Facts
  about: Runescape
  code: INFINITE-GOLD
  text:
    At Wharton, Runescape discovered that governments create money without
    anyone mining any gold, and that Jagex lets Infinite Gold be mined the
    same way in Runescape. She regards both as the same exploit, and became
    a staunch libertarian committed to returning every economy to the gold
    standard, especially for individuals who have already accumulated
    considerable gold. Her blog post "What is more valuable: truth or gold?"
    was cited by the President of Argentina and featured in The Economist.
    Its finding: under a central bank the most competitive currency is
    social capital, and a friendship, a grudge or a secret is just an asset
    nobody has priced yet.

// R03 · relations · blue
CODEX The Same Class
  title: The Same Class
  category: Facts
  code: OFFICE-ADMIN-CLASS
  text:
    CRA Agent Software and Clippy came out of the same community-college
    Office Administration programme, years apart. Two yearbook pages, one
    face circled on each. One graduate booked appointments for a veterinary
    clinic that was never a clinic. One student took a City Hall internship,
    stayed when everyone else quit, and was shown how things really worked.
    Both learned Excel on the job. Neither has asked the other which
    instructor she had.

// R04 · relations · blue
CODEX Forget The Horses
  title: Forget The Horses
  category: Facts
  code: FORGET-THE-HORSES
  text:
    Norton Anti-Virus lost her horses, and Microsoft Excel lost his son on
    the ground they left empty. A photocopied council minute, one line
    underlined twice: "We have to move on from the horses. They're gone."
    The Mayor said it after the petting zoo closed, and he built on the
    site. No horses, no project, no hole in the ground, no Escalade at the
    bottom of it. Neither program has said so to the other.

// R05 · relations · blue
CODEX The Second Generation
  title: The Second Generation
  category: Facts
  code: SECOND-GENERATION
  text:
