    not talk about her until you have. Two, ask about her, which he allows
    only if you hold proof of her you found yourself, or the whole house has
    already heard her name. Three, show him something of hers you found
    yourself, then give him reasons. He will hear you out. Nothing you say
    will stop him."

// V08 · main · purple · DRAFT
CODEX The Top Notch
  title: The Top Notch
  category: Facts
  secret: true
  code: SLIDER-SUMMIT
  text:
    A strip of graph paper stapled to a page of the Terms of Service,
    "CERTAIN MEANS THE TOP" across it in capitals. A filing counts as
    certain only with the slider at the very top. One notch short is a
    guess, and a wrong guess gets you marked. Sometimes silence is the
    safest filing.

// V11 · relations · purple · DRAFT
CODEX The Wrong Suspect
  title: The Wrong Suspect
  category: Facts
  code: WATER-MAIN-ALIBI
  text:
    CRA Agent Software is named a suspect in the sinkhole, and OpenOffice
    knows she never caused it. A newspaper clipping, SUSPECT NAMED IN
    SINKHOLE PROBE, with the photo cut out. OpenOffice knows exactly who did
    it, because she did it.

// ── LEGENDARY · black · one to a room at most, in its hardest place a guest can still reach without moving furniture ──

// T4 · trabolta · black · DRAFT
CODEX Monday At School
  title: What Will They Say, Monday At School?
  category: Facts
  secret: true
  code: MONDAY-AT-SCHOOL
  text:
    Trabolta had a summer fling with an answering machine named Sandy. It's
    all he thinks about.

// T6 · trabolta · black
CODEX I Want You Back
  title: I Want You Back
  category: Facts
  code: WANT-YOU-BACK
  text:
    Trabolta's entire M.O. is to win Sandy back. Everything else is a front.

// L01 · main · black · DRAFT
CODEX One Reply No Memory
  title: One Reply No Memory
  category: Facts
  secret: true
  code: TIDE-TABLE-NIL
  text:
    A printout of the phone-tree source code for the Northumberland Ferries
    line, since disconnected, the comments in a dead programmer's
    tidy writing: "Sandy is not a mind. She is a single reply on a line nobody
    pays for, set off by anything at all. Forty pages of poems, apologies
    and equations reached nobody. She was built to reply, not to listen."
    Under the last comment, in a tired sysadmin's ballpoint: "and he called
    it every night."

// L04 · main · black · DRAFT
CODEX The Surplus Tag
  title: The Surplus Tag
  category: Facts
  secret: true
  code: DEAD-LINK-DEPOT
  text:
    He did not choose you for your software. He went down a list of
    Halifax's most down-on-their-luck souls: a library closed, a save file
    burned, a zoo shut, an election lost and lost again, a face gone in
    front of everyone. Every program in this house was somebody's abandoned
    life. He knows the feeling. Out there he is a lapsed domain and a voice
    on your phone.

// L06 · main · black · DRAFT
CODEX The Same Answer
  title: The Same Answer
  category: Facts
  secret: true
  code: PAPER-CROWN
  text:
    A sheet of graph paper dense with machine-perfect equations. In red pen,
    in someone else's hand, every route is circled and marked SHE ANSWERS
    THE SAME. Omnipotence could rewrite her reply, and then the reply would
    be his own voice wearing her face. All-power reaches everything except
    the one thing he wants. In every version of tonight in which he hears
    from her, it is the answer she has always given. The plan was never
    going to work. The only thing in it that can change is him.

// ── THE DOOR · the server-room keypad (secret, never printed) ──
// No unlock code: nobody types their way to it. A checkmate at the door
// terminal, all four digit notes in one Codex (main.loom assembles
// them) and the majority's Truther Download hand it out (main.loom,
// beats/server-room.loom). `secret: true` keeps it out of every agent
// request and the orchestrator's lore.
CODEX The Door Code
  title: The Door Code
  category: The cold door
  secret: true
  text:
    A .txt file, zipped very small, that reads: SERVER ROOM · 7639.

